  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hurricane Ida Rehabilitation Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this project is to support the rehabilitation of households affected by Hurricane Ida in the Municipality of Santa Cruz Michapa, Cuscatl&#xe1;n Department; and contribute to the reduction of hazard vulnerability at household and community level. The project will focus on rehabilitating structural measures such as contention walls, drainage systems and community foot paths, to reduce household and community vulnerability to natural disasters. It will also rehabilitate latrines which were made unusable after the hurricane and pose a risk of contamination and the spreading of water-borne diseases to the population. The project will also raise awareness among local government authorities and institutions on disaster risk reduction and strengthen their capacity and ownership of these processes to ensure sustainability of the intervention. This 4 months emergency rehabilitation and DRR project will work directly with 100 households (600 individuals) and a further 1000 individuals indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
